1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,920
 I shouldn't be giving this away for free, but this is how to steal any cinematic color grade and apply it to your own video in under 60 seconds using AR.

2
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:10,900
 Pick a movie with a color grade you love. In my case, it's Batman.

3
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:16,000
 Step two is to Google Batman color palette and download a clean image of that palette.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,420
 Next, upload the palette image to ChatGPT and say, generate a LUT based on this color palette in a .cube extension.

5
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:28,600
 Assume you're the best colorist in the world. The LUT must work in a pro environment.

6
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:34,020
 Drop the file on an adjustment layout in Premiere and boom, you've got instantly cinematic vibes.

7
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:38,100
 If this saved you hours of trial and error, send this to a friend who needs better color grades.

